## Rules

- One visual at most once. Beat boundaries land at sentence/clause boundaries — you never write `start`/`end`: anchor each beat with its opening words (`marker`, verbatim from the cue lines) and optionally copy the cue seconds into `approx_start`. The first beat starts at the span start by construction — its `marker` should be the span's opening words.
- The first beat IS the hook: pick the visual whose subject matches the opening phrase.
- `motion` is one of `none` / `zoom_in` / `zoom_out` / `pan_left` / `pan_right`; `motion_rate` is the endpoint scale (1.05–1.20 when moving).
- `emphasis` is one of `none` / `hold` / `punch_in` / `caption_pop`; keep it scarce and vary the device.
- Mark `reset: true` on deliberate breathing shots (wider, slower, quieter).
- Every beat carries a one-line `note`: why this shot, here (evidence for review).

